---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/account.css';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Account"
  description="Connect Thiepn Library to your THIEPN Account and synchronize private reading state across devices."
  noindex
>
  <div class="page account-page">
    <section class="section account-shell" aria-labelledby="account-title">
      <header class="account-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">THIEPN Account</p>
        <h1 id="account-title">Account & sync</h1>
        <p data-account-summary>Checking account status…</p>
      </header>

      <div class="account-card" data-account-signed-out hidden>
        <h2>Keep reading without an account</h2>
        <p>Library remains fully usable as a local-first reader. If THIEPN Account is already signed in, Library connects automatically. You can also connect manually without signing into Library separately.</p>
        <button type="button" class="account-primary" data-account-action data-sign-in>Connect THIEPN Account</button>
      </div>

      <div class="account-card" data-account-signed-in hidden>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Signed in</p>
          <h2 data-account-name>THIEPN Account</h2>
          <p data-account-email></p>
        </div>
        <div class="account-actions">
          <a href="https://account.thiepn.dev/" rel="noopener">Manage THIEPN Account</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="account-card sync-card" data-sync-panel hidden aria-labelledby="sync-title">
        <div class="sync-card__heading">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Private cloud sync</p>
            <h2 id="sync-title">Library reading state</h2>
          </div>
          <strong data-sync-mode>Local-only on this device</strong>
        </div>

        <p data-sync-status>Your local reading data will not be uploaded until you enable sync.</p>
        <p class="micro" data-sync-meta>No cloud sync enabled.</p>
        <div class="sync-device-preferences" data-auto-sync-section hidden>
          <div>
            <strong>Automatically sync this device</strong>
            <p class="micro">When enabled, Library checks for changes every 30 seconds while this tab is visible and online. It also syncs after local edits and reconnecting. Turning this off keeps manual sync available.</p>
          </div>
          <label class="sync-device-switch">
            <input type="checkbox" data-auto-sync-checkbox aria-describedby="auto-sync-status" />
            <span>Auto-sync</span>
          </label>
          <p id="auto-sync-status" data-auto-sync-status role="status">Checking device preference…</p>
          <p data-auto-sync-runtime role="status" aria-live="polite">No foreground check yet in this tab.</p>
        </div>

        <section class="sync-boundary" data-core-coordinate-section hidden aria-labelledby="core-coordinate-title">
          <h3 id="core-coordinate-title">Core sync coordination · this device</h3>
          <p class="micro">Optional, separate from Library cloud sync. Allows a Core coordination request to ask Library to check through its existing Account sync engine. Does not share reading records with Core or make other apps automatically sync.</p>
          <label class="sync-device-switch">
            <input type="checkbox" data-core-coordinate-toggle aria-describedby="core-coordinate-status" />
            <span>Allow requests to Library from Core</span>
          </label>
          <p id="core-coordinate-status" data-core-coordinate-status role="status">Coordination is off.</p>
          <p class="micro" data-core-coordinate-guidance>Native Library owns every sync and recovery operation.</p>
          <p class="micro"><a href={`${base}/backup`}>Export or restore a Library backup</a> · <a href="https://account.thiepn.dev/privacy/apps/library" rel="noopener">Review Library cloud deletion</a></p>
          <button type="button" data-account-action data-core-coordinate-request>Request native Library sync</button>
          <p class="micro">To revoke, turn this switch off. If Library has a conflict, resolve it with Library's source-of-truth chooser above.</p>
        </section>
        <div class="account-actions">
          <button type="button" class="account-primary" data-account-action data-sync-enable>Sync this device</button>
          <div data-sync-enabled-actions hidden>
            <button type="button" class="account-primary" data-account-action data-sync-now>Sync now</button>
            <button type="button" data-account-action data-sync-pause>Pause sync</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <section class="sync-boundary" data-recovery-center aria-labelledby="library-recovery-heading">
          <h3 id="library-recovery-heading">Recovery inspection</h3>
          <p class="micro">Check this device's real Library Account baseline, native sync state, offline status and Core permission. Inspection does not initiate cloud writes or certify independent offsite custody.</p>
          <div class="account-actions">
            <button data-account-action data-recovery-inspect type="button">Inspect recovery state</button>
            <button data-account-action data-recovery-revoke type="button">Revoke Core coordination</button>
            <a data-recovery-backup href={`${base}/backup`}>Native Library backup &amp; restore</a>
          </div>
          <p data-recovery-inspection role="status" aria-live="polite">No recovery inspection performed. Local reading is available without a Core grant.</p>
          <p class="micro" data-recovery-cas>Native CAS revisions are displayed after an original Library sync or conflict choice.</p>
          <button type="button" data-account-action data-recovery-post-choice>Recheck Library's native heads after any conflict choice</button>
          <p class="micro" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-recovery-after-choice>No original post-choice comparison performed in this tab.</p>
          <p class="micro" data-recovery-history-empty>No native recovery incidents recorded in this tab.</p>
          <ol data-recovery-history aria-label="Local recovery incident history"></ol>
          <div data-recovery-conflict-actions hidden>
            <p class="micro">Conflict recovery: export a backup before selecting the authoritative copy with the native chooser below.</p>
          </div>
        </section>
        <aside class="sync-conflict" data-sync-conflict hidden>
          <h3>Choose the source of truth</h3>
          <button type="button" data-account-action data-recovery-compare-heads>Compare this device and cloud changes</button>
          <p class="micro" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-recovery-heads>No native snapshot comparison performed. No records are exposed by comparison.</p>
          <p>Changes were made both here and in the cloud. Automatic synchronization pauses to protect both versions. Review which copy should become authoritative.</p>
          <p class="micro">Using this device replaces the cloud snapshot. To use cloud, first create and save an original-format safety backup. Library checks both the cloud revision and device state again immediately before the native restore; a changed head stops recovery.</p>
          <button type="button" data-account-action data-recovery-prepare-cloud>Prepare cloud restore &amp; download local backup</button>
          <button type="button" data-account-action data-recovery-prepare-device>Prepare device publish &amp; download cloud safety copy</button>
          <p class="micro" data-recovery-device-preparation role="status" aria-live="polite">Before using this device to replace an existing cloud snapshot, request and save a separate copy of that cloud snapshot.</p>
          <p class="micro" data-recovery-preparation role="status" aria-live="polite">No native safety backup prepared in this tab.</p>
          <input type="file" accept=".json,application/json" data-recovery-saved-file aria-label="Select a saved Library JSON safety backup" hidden />
          <div class="account-actions">
            <button type="button" data-account-action data-recovery-verify-device>Validate saved cloud safety file</button>
            <button type="button" data-account-action data-recovery-verify-cloud>Validate saved device safety file</button>
          </div>
          <p class="micro" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-recovery-saved-device>No saved cloud safety file verified yet.</p>
          <p class="micro" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-recovery-saved-cloud>No saved device safety file verified yet.</p>
          <p class="micro">File inspection uses Library's original JSON validator and compares only its canonical snapshot hash with the current one-use preparation. Choosing Device or Cloud requires a matching selected file. Nothing is uploaded or imported by inspection. A matching file on this device does not prove independent external backup retention.</p>

          <div class="account-actions">
            <button type="button" class="account-primary" data-account-action data-use-device>Use this device</button>
            <button type="button" data-account-action data-use-cloud>Use cloud</button>
          </div>
        </aside>

        <div class="sync-boundary">
          <h3>What reading-state sync includes</h3>
          <p>Saved books, EPUB/PDF progress, bookmarks, highlights, notes, reading activity, reader settings, and portable personal-book metadata.</p>
          <p><strong>Personal EPUB/PDF bytes are never placed inside the reading-state snapshot.</strong> File continuity is a separate permission below. Local cover blobs remain device-local.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="sync-boundary personal-file-cloud" aria-labelledby="personal-file-cloud-title">
          <div class="sync-card__heading">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">Optional file continuity</p>
              <h3 id="personal-file-cloud-title">Personal book cloud</h3>
            </div>
            <strong data-personal-files-mode>Checking…</strong>
          </div>
          <p data-personal-files-status>Checking private-file permission…</p>
          <p class="micro" data-personal-files-summary>Personal files are separate from reading-state sync.</p>

          <div data-personal-files-disabled>
            <p>When you explicitly allow this sensitive permission in THIEPN Account, Library can privately store personal EPUB/PDF files up to 50 MB so another signed-in device can restore them automatically after metadata sync.</p>
            <a href="https://account.thiepn.dev/apps/library" rel="noopener">Manage Personal book cloud permission</a>
          </div>

          <div data-personal-files-enabled hidden>
            <div class="account-actions">
              <button type="button" class="account-primary" data-account-action data-personal-files-sync>Sync personal books now</button>
              <a href="https://account.thiepn.dev/apps/library" rel="noopener">Manage permission</a>
            </div>
            <p class="micro">Objects are private, owner-scoped, and named by SHA-256. Books over 50 MB remain device-local and can still be relinked by importing the original file.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <section class="sync-boundary ecosystem-overview" aria-labelledby="ecosystem-sync-heading" data-ecosystem-sync-overview>
          <h3 id="ecosystem-sync-heading">Ecosystem sync dashboard</h3>
          <p class="micro">Each app owns its data, permissions and sync engine. Library cannot check another app's private sync status without its own consent.</p>
          <div class="ecosystem-app-grid">
            <article aria-labelledby="ecosystem-library">
              <h4 id="ecosystem-library">Library</h4>
              <p data-ecosystem-library-state role="status">Checking this device…</p>
              <p class="micro" data-ecosystem-library-detail>Reading-state sync uses Library's own Account permission.</p>
              <button type="button" data-account-action data-ecosystem-retry>Check Library again</button>
            </article>
            <article aria-labelledby="ecosystem-notes">
              <h4 id="ecosystem-notes">Notes</h4>
              <p>Managed independently by Notes.</p>
              <p class="micro">Open Notes → Settings → Account &amp; sync to see its native status and Core coordination permission. No Notes records are read here.</p>
              <a href="/notes/" rel="noopener">Open Notes</a>
            </article>
            <article aria-labelledby="ecosystem-hub">
              <h4 id="ecosystem-hub">Hub</h4>
              <p>Metadata sharing requires its own consent.</p>
              <p class="micro">Hub remains a temporary read-only device session. It does not receive Library cloud copies.</p>
              <a href="/" rel="noopener">Open Hub</a>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>
        <div class="danger-zone">
          <h3>Cloud-data lifecycle</h3>
          <p>Deletion is managed centrally by THIEPN Account with a deletion review, recent-authentication check, and revision-conflict protection. Local reading data and personal files on this device are not erased.</p>
          <a href="https://account.thiepn.dev/privacy/apps/library" rel="noopener">Manage Library cloud data in THIEPN Account</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <p><a href={`${base}/backup`}>Manual backup & restore</a> remains available independently of Account sync.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <script>
    import { mountLibraryAccountPage } from '../lib/account/account-dom';
    const unmount = mountLibraryAccountPage();
    window.addEventListener('pagehide', unmount, { once: true });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
